HST Office: the ribbon's groups are fitted again when the banner's room changes and the box keeps its size.

The tab's ladder fits its groups in Resize, at the box's width plus the room the banner may give back
(SetPageSlack). When the banner took or gave back room and the box kept its size, no Resize followed and the groups
stayed fitted at the old width: on Linux, Sheets › Chèn after the window grew from 1366 to 1920 px had every group
large, 1560 px in a 1515 px track, its last group 23 px past the banner's margin. HstSetSlack now fits the groups
again at once. The layout dump gives the box's "ladder_width" (the width of the last fit) and "large_natural" (the
tab's widest large button at that fit, logical px: a label wider than 96 px widens the large buttons of a wide tab
beyond 96 rather than being cut, Linux's UI font at 125 %).

- vcl/source/control/HstRibbonV3MergedBox.cxx (HstSetSlack, HstApplyV3, HstDump), vcl/inc/PriorityMergedHBox.hxx.

License: these upstream-derived files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
Test: tests/unit/test_ribbon_ladder_follows_slack.py; tests/runtime/check-ribbon-v3-dumps.py on Linux gtk3 at 1366
and 1920 (clip, widening).

